  "worked_solution": "Both the numerator and denominator approach $\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$ However, since ${e}^{2x}\u226b\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(6x)$ for large values of $x,$ the numerator is growing much faster than the denominator. Consequently, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{{e}^{2x}}{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(6x)}=\\infty .\n$$",
